  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies hybrid quantum reservoir computing for credit-card default prediction using QuEra Aquila with 12-feature detuning encoding and 13-feature position encoding over 5 timesteps, with 240 shots selected for hardware runs. On CARDS_30000, the best reported F1-score is 0.57 in emulation, while on CARDS_1000 the best reported F1-score reaches 0.71; the paper also reports that hardware noise and decoherence reduce performance relative to noiseless emulation, and that the quantum results are broadly comparable to classical baselines rather than clearly superior.",
